    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the driveway so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly on both sides, as the single access point must be immediately visible to arriving units.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the long driveway to maintain a clear travel path wide enough for emergency vehicles.\n• Cut back any tree branches overhanging the driveway to allow full-height clearance for fire apparatus and ambulances.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of parked vehicles so arriving units can reach the residence without stopping to reposition.\n• Mark the boundary of the water feature nearest the driveway or turnaround area so responders working in low-light or smoky conditions do not approach it unknowingly.\n• Designate and mark a flat staging area away from the water feature where responders can position equipment and personnel.\n• Use the circular driveway as the primary turnaround point and keep it free of vehicles, decorative objects, and stored items at all times.\n• Post a simple diagram of the property layout, including the detached structure location and circular driveway, at the road entrance or on a weatherproof box near the driveway entry.\n• Confirm the detached structure has a visible address or unit identifier so responders can distinguish it from the main residence during an emergency"
  },
