    "recommendations": "• Trim all shrubs that are growing directly next to the house so there is open ground between the plants and the walls.\n• Remove or cut back brush in the areas immediately surrounding the structure to create open, clear ground around the building.\n• Thin scattered shrubs within the yard to increase the open space between individual plants and the house.\n• Clear brush from both sides of the driveway so vehicles can pass through without vegetation contact and so the route stays open during an emergency.\n• Trim any tree branches that hang over or touch the house, roof, or deck.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure so their branches do not touch each other or extend over the building.\n• Remove dead or dry plant material from within the mixed vegetation areas closest to the structure.\n• Keep the driveway free of fallen branches, overgrown shrubs, and other debris along its full length.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is visible to emergency vehicles approaching from the road.\n• Maintain the single access route by keeping vegetation cut back on both sides from the road to the house.\n• Move any cut brush, wood piles, or loose yard debris away from the house and outbuildings.\n• Keep vegetation thinned and low in the open terrain areas closest to the structure so fire has less material to carry toward the building.\n• Keep the area around the water feature clear of accumulated dead"
  },
